 trials (reviewed in Roskoski, 2019). Dual mechanism inhibitors, including the ATP-competitive inhibitors SCH772984 and MK-8353, bind to the unphosphorylated MAPK and prevent both its own kinase activity and its phosphorylation by MAP2Ks (Morris et al, 2013; Deng et al 2014; Chaikuad et al, 2014; Boga et al, 2018; Moschos et al, 2019; reviewed in Samatar and Poulikakos, 2014). MAPK inhibitors offer the potential to mitigate the development of resistance to RAF and MAP2K inhibitors, which often involves reactivation of MAPK-dependent signaling. As a result, MAPK inhibitors are frequently used in combination with RAF and MAP2K-directed therapeutics (reviewed in Samatar and Poulikakos, 2014; Roskoski, 2019). ", "className": "Summation", "schemaClass": "Summation"}], "reviewStatus": {"dbId": 9821382, "displayName": "five stars", "definition": "externally reviewed", "name": ["five stars"], "className": "ReviewStatus", "schemaClass": "ReviewStatus"}, "isChimeric": false, "category": "binding", "input": [{"dbId": 5672723, "displayName": "activated RAF:scaffold:p-2S MAP2K:MAPK complex [plasma membrane]", "stId": "R-HSA-5672723", "stIdVersion": "R-HSA-5672723.1", "maxDepth": 11, "name": ["activated RAF:scaffold:p-2S MAP2K:MAPK complex"], "speciesName": "Homo sapiens", "catalystActivities": [{"dbId": 5672974, "displayName": "protein serine/threonine kinase activity of activated RAF:scaffold:p-2S MAP2K:MAPK complex [plasma membrane]", "physicalEntity": 5672723, "className": "CatalystActivity", "schemaClass": "CatalystActivity"}], "consumedByEvent": [9657603], "isChimeric": false, "species": [48887], "inDisease": false, "schemaClass": "Complex", "className": "Complex"}, {"dbId": 9657570, "displayName": "dual mechanism MAPK inhibitors [cytosol]", "stId": "R-ALL-9657570", "stIdVersion": "R-ALL-9657570.1", "maxDepth": 2, "name": ["dual mechanism MAPK inhibitors"], "crossReference": [{"dbId": 12020745, "displayName": "Mondo:0004992", "databaseName": "Mondo", "identifier": "0004992"